From 18055baa650028e36b4866df8cff97cd111ec6cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Yin <peter.yin@quantatw.com>
Date: Mon, 19 May 2025 15:12:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] psu: support gpio bridge

Support for GPIO bridge is required for certain components that
need a GPIO to be set before reading, such as battery voltage.
To obtain a valid reading, the BridgeGpio option can be configured
in the Entity Manager JSON, similar to the implementation used for
ADC sensors.

Tested
entity-manager configuration
"BridgeGpio": [
    {
        "Label": "in0",
        "Name": "battery-read-en",
        "Polarity": "High",
        "SetupTime": 1
    }
],

xyz.openbmc_project.
Configuration.
ADC128D818.BridgeGpio0 interface -  -                 -
.Label                 property  s  "in0"             emits-change
.Name                  property  s  "battery-read-en" emits-change
.Polarity              property  s  "High"            emits-change
.SetupTime             property  t  1                 emits-change

root@bmc:~# busctl introspect xyz.openbmc_project.PSUSensor
/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/voltage/MB_P3V_BAT_VOLT_V
xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Value

NAME      TYPE      SIGNATURE RESULT/VALUE
.MaxValue property  d         255
.MinValue property  d         0
.Unit     property  s         "xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Value.Unit
.Value    property  d         3.024

